## Vendored-data provenance

`src/spectralData.ts` contains reflectance and colour-matching data derived
from **rvanwijnen/spectral.js** (https://github.com/rvanwijnen/spectral.js),
licensed under the **MIT License** above.

Vendored tables:

- `BASE_SPECTRA` — published reflectance curves for the six spectral.js
  primaries (W/C/M/Y/R/G/B) sampled at 38 bands (380–750 nm).
- `CIE_CMF` — CIE 1931 colour-matching functions used to reconstruct
  linear sRGB from a reflectance curve.
- `CONVERSION` — the sRGB linear <-> XYZ matrices used in that reconstruction.

`src/mix.ts` is a method-level port of the published Kubelka-Munk mixing
math (`KS` / `KM` / spectral upsampling / `mix`) from the same MIT upstream.
No code is copied or transliterated from `SPECS/v1.1.0-water-color/watercolor-playground/`
(msurguy/watercolor-playground) or `johnowhitaker/inkwash` — both unlicensed —
per the Phase 56 clean-room law (P1 / D-17). No Mixbox code, LUTs, or spectra
are present in this package (P2).
